    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0841" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg771"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States, Lima,
                                Peru,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 14, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith the
                    copy and translation of a despatch received, on the 6th instant, from his
                    excellency the minister of foreign <pb facs="0842" n="772" xml:id="pg772"/>
                    affairs, informing me of a law passed by the congress of Peru, obliging the
                    executive to continue the war against Spain, and at the same time sending me a
                    copy of the said law, which I likewise transmit, with translation.</p>
                <p>This information was laid before the department by me, in my despatch of May
                    28th, 1867, No. 68, but I am now informed of it officially for the first
                    time.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALVIN P. HOVEY.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d474-a1.xml" xpointer="d474-a1"/>
